      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T22:22:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Judging from [this code](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:art/runtime/runtime.cc;l\u003d1515-1521;drc\u003dfc2f6b36c4d23dc70e1b7c2122890bb8ecc9c834), this \"APEX version\" is either a millisecond timestamp or an actual APEX version.\n\nSince a timestamp isn\u0027t an \"APEX version\", and what actually is is well established, I find this confusing, and I think it\u0027s unfortunate that the confusion gets finalised in the file format. I suggest making this `apex-timestamps` and have a TODO to refactor the internals to clean up the terminology.\n\n(Granted `apex-timestamps` isn\u0027t 100% correct either, but it\u0027s a different and largely unused term and hence much less confusing, and something like `apex-timestamps-or-versions` gets too clunky imo.)",
